By \hyperref[rec:PSC-I-T-MODULE-TOP]{
olinkurl{PSC-I-T-MODULE-TOP}}, $\srank_A(M)=\srank_{A/J}(M/JM)$.  Apply \hyperref[rec:PSC-I-T-SEMISIMPLE-SEED-RANK]{
olinkurl{PSC-I-T-SEMISIMPLE-SEED-RANK}} to the displayed decompositions of $A/J$ and $M/JM$, with every $D_i= bk$.  This gives the stated maximum.  If $q=0$, the unital $A/J$-module $M/JM$ is zero, and \hyperref[rec:PSC-I-T-MODULE-TOP]{
olinkurl{PSC-I-T-MODULE-TOP}} gives seed rank zero.
